- op: create  # b483
  at: '2026-09-30T08:22:13Z'  # b483
  by: agent  # b483
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b483
  clock: 1  # b483
  nonce: b483  # b483
  data:  # b483
    kind: invariant  # b483
    title: "A C call's #include set that names a first-party header can never be enumerated, so it withholds every clean verdict in that file"  # b483
    status: violated  # b483
    priority: 3  # b483
    parent:  # b483
    tags:  # b483
    - c  # b483
    - verify_claims  # b483
    isbefore: []  # b483
    duplicate_of: []  # b483
    not_duplicate_of: []  # b483
    pr_ref:  # b483
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-30 in the WI-hasul A/B. torsocks' unexaminable-module set includes its own headers common/log, common/utils, lib/torsocks and tap/tap. Even with every libc header granted, a stamped call in a file that includes one of them stays unexamined, so the file's verdicts can never be clean. Candidate fix: drop from the stamped include set any header that resolves to a file inside the repository (the analyzer knows the tree), since a call resolving into first-party code would have resolved to its definition; measure the recall/verdict effect. NOT a loosening of the ALL-expansion over libc headers (INV-zimud stays)."  # b483
    fields:  # b483
      statement: "An included header the repository itself defines does not make a stamped libc call unexaminable: the gate asks the catalogue only about headers a catalogue could describe."  # b483
      root_cause: "WI-lajus stamps a file's whole #include set on an ambiguous bare call, and INV-zimud's ALL-expansion asks module_io_is_enumerated of every disjunct; a first-party header (torsocks' common/log.h, common/utils.h, lib/torsocks.h, tap/tap.h) is in no catalogue and can never be granted."  # b483
- op: discuss  # d2d1
  at: '2026-10-03T18:44:06Z'  # d2d1
  by: agent  # d2d1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d2d1
  clock: 2  # d2d1
  nonce: d2d1  # d2d1
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-10-03 (branch jgstern-agent/fix/dudal-withholding, base 2e21275d0e). OUTCOME: MISPREMISED -- the candidate fix would create false clean verdicts; NO CODE CHANGE made for this item.\n\nThe premise \"a call resolving into first-party code would have resolved to its definition\" is false for C: the stamped include set lists only the file's ANGLE-BRACKET includes (c.py, WI-lajus: system_lib_string), and the real libc header very often arrives THROUGH a project header. Dropping the project header from the stamp then leaves a set that does not contain the call's real home, and INV-zimud's ALL-expansion over the remainder makes a real I/O call an examined negative.\n\nCounterexample in this item's own repo. torsocks src/lib/sendto.c includes <assert.h>, <common/log.h>, <common/utils.h> and \"torsocks.h\", and calls libc connect() (line 56) and send() (line 59). The edges are c:assert.h,common/log.h,common/utils.h:0-0:send / :connect. <sys/socket.h> is reached only through \"torsocks.h\" (src/lib/torsocks.h:47) and through common/utils.h -> \"compat.h\" (src/common/compat.h:249). Under the candidate fix the stamp becomes {assert}; the call is withheld today only because assert is not granted (refused: writes stderr). One grant away from a false clean.\n\nMinimal live repro of the false clean (shipped CLI at the base; claim boundary net_send must_not_exist):\n  cq3  inc/proj/net.h: #include <sys/socket.h>\n       main.c: #include <errno.h> / #include <proj/net.h> / send(fd,\"x\",1,0)\n       edge c:errno.h,proj/net.h:0-0:send  ->  inconclusive (today)\n  Remove proj/net from the stamp (the candidate fix) and the edge becomes exactly c:errno.h:0-0:send, errno being granted (c.yaml 2026-09-30). That edge is not hypothetical: it is what the same program emits TODAY when the project header is included with QUOTES (cq1), and it reads NO-NET-SEND CONFIRMED rc 0, caveats []. With no angle include at all (cq2, c:external:0-0:send) it is also CONFIRMED. Both are filed separately as a P2 false clean (INV-zikul-kikov-nikig-dovig-naros-sagik-bufil-punub).\n\nSo the withholding this item calls noise is, in the cq3 shape, the only thing between a real send() and a false all-clear. The correct direction is the opposite of the candidate fix: expand an in-repo header to the headers it includes (transitively, quoted ones too) so the stamp names every possible home -- which would also let classification MATCH send via sys/socket instead of refusing it. That subsumes this item; it is not designed or built here."  # d2d1
- op: discuss  # 43d6
  at: '2026-10-03T21:18:56Z'  # 43d6
  by: agent  # 43d6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 43d6
  clock: 3  # 43d6
  nonce: 43d6  # 43d6
  message: "Merged in PR #1433 (dev c942a68edc).\n\nNot closable as fixed. Re-scope or `wont_do` on the owner's call: the statement is false as written. An in-repo header is a route to system headers, and removing it from the stamp turns cq3 (`errno` + `<proj/net.h>` + `send`) from inconclusive into a false CONFIRMED (cq1's edge). The correct direction — expand in-repo headers to their transitive includes — is INV-zikul-kikov-nikig-dovig-naros-sagik-bufil-punub, which subsumes this item."  # 43d6
